\section{Caveats}{
\itemize{
\item Units are years: month 1/12, week 7/365.25, day 1/365.25, hour 1/(365.25 x 24).
\item A bare number (63, 11\% of real corpus age cells) is refused, never assumed to be years.
\item years for a wide Range is a poor stand-in for any one sample; filter on precision.
\item Every cell costs one line, not one process: send all cells in one call.
}
}
\section{Performance}{
Every call starts one bridge process, which costs a .NET start-up before any work. 
}
